{"id":"u-13dd849f-d84d-4c61-8ca6-a7fa142a84dd","src":"community","title":"Oak & Iron: Beginner’s Forge","author":"Tank","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/kANz7r-oak-and-iron-the-first-pull","desc":"Welcome to the Forge.\n\nA youth strength program built for young warriors learning the ancient art of picking heavy things up correctly while making unnecessary sound effects in the garage.\n\nThis isn’t PE class.\nThis isn’t “functional movement enrichment.”\nAnd this definitely isn’t an iPad workout.\n\nBeginner’s Forge is a home-grown strength program designed to help kids build:\n\n* real-world strength\n* coordination\n* confidence\n* grit\n* and elite-level grocery carrying capabilities\n\nInside Oak & Iron, strength is earned the old-fashioned way:\nthrough reps, consistency, and mildly concerning enthusiasm for deadlifts.\n\nYoung lifters will learn:\n\n* proper hinge mechanics\n* squatting patterns\n* carries\n* hangs\n* crawling\n* core stability\n* and how to become suspiciously strong for their age without turning into little gym psychos\n\nEvery session is short, simple, and intentionally built for growing bodies and attention spans that may abruptly disappear after spotting a squirrel outside.\n\nThe mission is simple:\nBuild strong kids.\nBuild steady confidence.\nBuild memories in the garage that last longer than the soreness.\n\nNo gimmicks.\nNo screaming coaches.\nNo fake alpha nonsense.\n\nJust iron, wood, hard work, and the occasional chocolate milk-fueled PR attempt while Dad nods approvingly from across the rack like a woodland strength wizard.\n\nBecause at Oak & Iron…\nstrength doesn’t arrive overnight.\n\nIt takes root.","level":["Beginner"],"goals":["Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":20,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-05-15T00:14:03.768Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Jumping Jack","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Squat (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":5